=== Implication: c-map = edge-shift on Euler bricks ===
Each c-map output is a primitive Euler brick (a, b, c) with a:b = 1:q,
c being recovered from a MW generator of E_PCP(q).

The Euler-brick K3 V' has rho(V') >= 10. Its Picard lattice acts on rational
points of V'. The c-map orbit graph is a SECTION of one such Picard action.

Specifically: V' has 3 elliptic fibrations pi_a, pi_b, pi_c (one per edge).
Each fibration has sections forming a Mordell-Weil lattice.
The c-map is the composition: take a section s of pi_a, evaluate its
c-coordinate, which gives a point on a DIFFERENT fiber of pi_a OR a section
of pi_c. This is exactly the action of a specific Picard element.
